        "content": [
          {
            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "**Elon Musk's xAI announcements** primarily revolve around the company's founding in 2023 as a \"maximum truth-seeking AI\" alternative to competitors like OpenAI, the development of its Grok chatbot series (including Grok-1.5 in 2024 with improved coding/math capabilities), and major corporate moves in 2025–2026.[[1]](https://www.reuters.com/technology/musks-xai-launch-improved-version-chatbot-2024-03-29/)\n\nKey recent developments include:\n\n- **Mergers and rebranding**: In early 2026, SpaceX acquired xAI, forming a combined entity valued at around $1.25 trillion (later rising post-IPO). This integrated AI (Grok), rockets, Starlink, and X (formerly Twitter, which xAI had previously acquired in 2025 for ~$33 billion). The merged company was later officially renamed **SpaceXAI** in July 2026, with a new logo and X account (@SpaceXAI). The goal is to build massive space-based data centers for cheaper AI compute, potentially the lowest-cost option within 2–3 years, enabling Moon/Mars expansion and beyond.[[2]](https://www.theverge.com/tech/872619/elon-musk-merges-spacex-with-xai-and-x)[[3]](https://mashable.com/tech/xai-spacexai-name)[[4]](https://apnews.com/article/spacex-xai-musk-space-2079f03fa888652b7fe836afe8b670a1)\n\n- **Reorganization and ambitions**: Following the merger, Musk restructured xAI (now under the combined entity) in February 2026, parting ways with several co-founders (leaving about half the original 12). The company split into focused teams: Grok (chatbot/voice), coding, Imagine (video/image generation), and Macrohard (AI for automating companies/coding). Musk publicly shared a 45-minute all-hands meeting emphasizing interplanetary AI infrastructure, including a lunar factory, mass driver (electromagnetic catapult) for AI satellites, and capturing solar energy on a massive scale. He described it as leading to self-sustaining lunar cities before Mars and \"incredibly exciting\" super-scale intelligence.[[5]](https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/11/xai-lays-out-interplanetary-ambitions-in-public-all-hands/)[[6]](https://www.reuters.com/business/musk-says-xai-was-reorganized-2026-02-11/)[[7]](https://www.ft.com/content/758b3d7d-e94f-40ba-b705-23341ca9bdfe)\n\n- **Other notable projects**: In late 2025, Musk announced a massive 500 MW xAI data center in Saudi Arabia (powered by Nvidia chips, larger than its Colossus cluster in Memphis) alongside plans for solar-powered AI satellites. xAI has also pushed \"truth-seeking\" AI, open-sourced early models, and focused on multimodal capabilities like image/video generation.[[8]](https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/elon-musk-announces-massive-xai-data-center-saudi-arabia-x-rcna244804)\n\nThese moves position the combined SpaceXAI as a vertically integrated powerhouse for AI, space, and real-time information, with an IPO in 2026 that significantly boosted its valuation. For the absolute latest or primary sources, check Musk's or @xAI/@SpaceXAI posts on X, or official announcements on x.ai or spacex.com.",
